  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "NOAK capital cost reaches 50-60% of FOAK through fleet learning, bringing specific cost from €15,000-18,000/kWe down to €7,500-9,000/kWe",
      "Non-planar HTS stellarator coils (55 mm / 100 kA) can be manufactured at 18 m major radius scale with ~10,000 demountable joints maintaining ~1 nΩ resistance",
      "Steady-state disruption-free operation delivers 85-90% capacity factor despite complex 3D blanket maintenance geometry",
      "REBCO HTS supply chain scales from thousands of km/year to 26,000+ km per plant at $5-10/kA-m (vs current $30-100/kA-m)",
      "Breeding blanket achieves TBR > 1.05 in realistic HELIAS 3D geometry with 80 unique segment shapes and 20 mm inter-segment gaps",
      "Dual LTS/HTS conductor strategy resolves to a production choice that keeps magnet costs within NOAK learning curve projections"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No current-drive system required — saves ~50-200 MW recirculating power and eliminates central solenoid magnet cost",
      "No disruption mitigation infrastructure — avoids PFC overdesign, unplanned outage costs, and disruption-induced component replacement",
      "No thermal energy storage buffer needed for pulsed operation (estimated $50-200M for grid-scale storage in pulsed tokamaks)",
      "Longer blanket component lifetime (4.6-9 years vs 2.3 years for DEMO tokamak) reduces number of replacement campaigns from ~17 to ~8 over plant life"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "3D non-planar modular coil fabrication at 18 m scale: 40 coils in 5 shapes, ~300 tonnes each, with tolerances compounding nonlinearly — no manufacturing precedent beyond W7-X at 5.5 m",
      "Complex 3D blanket with 640 unique segments (80 per sector × 8 sectors) requiring diverse fabrication tooling and undefined remote maintenance procedures",
      "~10,000 demountable superconducting joints per machine requiring nΩ-class resistance stability over decades under neutron irradiation",
      "26 million meters of REBCO HTS tape per plant — exceeding current global annual production by >10× — or alternatively 800 tonnes of Nb3Sn with strain-sensitive non-planar winding"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "FOAK capital cost of €15-18B (€15,000-18,000/kWe) with no published NOAK learning projection — LCOE remains above $150/MWh if NOAK fraction exceeds 70%",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Blanket type (HCPB vs DCLL) undisclosed — determines thermal efficiency (35% vs 40%+), power cycle, TBR margin, and propagates ~20-25% LCOE uncertainty",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "18 m major radius is 3× ITER scale — coil system mass ~35,000 tonnes, shipping/assembly logistics unstudied, tolerances compound nonlinearly",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Blanket Segment 5 fails RCC-MRx structural criterion under accident loads — no published resolution",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO supply chain requires >10× current global production capacity for a single plant, with cost needing to drop 3-20× from current prices",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Blanket maintenance scheme explicitly undefined — 640 unique segments in 3D geometry with no published remote handling procedure or cycle time estimate",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Demountable joint technology at 100 kA / ~1 nΩ unproven at production scale — resistance stability under neutron irradiation and thermal cycling unknown",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "QI non-planar design path may carry structural capital cost disadvantage vs QA planar-coil stellarators (Helios at 8 m) — a design-space risk not recoverable through learning",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "No published O&M cost breakdown for HELIAS or GIGA — placeholder 2-4% of NOAK capital is the only viable estimate",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Realistic TBR (~1.15) has limited margin over unity when accounting for geometric penalties from 3D blanket gaps",
        "severity": "medium"
      }
    ]
  },
